phis (0.2.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Jobs: Core keeps the clock. A job declares a schedule (5m, 15m, 30m, hourly, daily, weekly, with a
    time of day for the daily and weekly steps) and every serving instance claims each moment of it by
    a row in phis.job_runs; the unique key on the moment admits one instance, which runs the job under a
    lease the others take over if it dies, and a moment during a running run is recorded as skipped.
    The latest missed moment runs once at the next start. phis addon jobs reads the ledger, phis addon
    job --pause | --resume switches a job, phis addon job runs one now through the same ledger.
  * Jobs: the Add-on event outbox and the notification outbox are drained every five minutes by Core's
    own jobs, and the ledger is pruned daily; the operator's timers for phis addon job and phis mail
    drain are no longer needed. phis maintain keeps its timer.
  * Events: an Add-on emits events under its own id (@scope/name:event), declared in emits and sent
    through the events:v1 capability; Core writes one outbox row per listening Add-on with emitter, hop
    and dedupe key and delivers them as its own events. A chain of handlers ends at four hops.
  * Schema: phis.job_runs and phis.job_states are new, created by phis schema apply. The outbox columns
    emitter, hop and dedupe_key, its widened subject check and the dedupe index are declared in the
    creation script; an outbox created before them is brought to that shape by hand (DB.md).
  * Depends on @phis/contracts 0.7.4 (job schedules, emitted events).

 -- Phisys Ltd. <debian@phisys.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 10:39:13 +0000

phis (0.2.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Site search: Core keeps the page texts of a Site's Public and App Areas, per locale, as one set
    under a fingerprint the Site computes (phis.site_search_sets, phis.site_search_documents), and
    answers a query with ranked hits and highlighted snippets: Postgres full text with prefix matching,
    the title weighing more than the description and the body. The Site extracts the texts and hands
    them in; Core refuses a set for any other Area. A set whose fingerprint Core already holds is not
    written again. SEARCH.md describes the split; the API reference carries the three endpoints.
  * Site API: the Area endpoint lists the published pages of App as it did of Public, which the Site's
    indexer reads.
  * Schema: the two search tables are new; `phis schema apply` creates them on an existing installation.
  * Depends on @phis/contracts 0.7.3 (the search contract).

 -- Phisys Ltd. <debian@phisys.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 07:53:36 +0000

phis (0.2.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: config/phis-runtime.json, which holds the database passwords and the API tokens, is
    written with mode 0600. Every write replaced it with a file carrying the umask's mode (usually
    0644), so it was world-readable after db bootstrap, the setup pages or any CLI command that writes
    the configuration, even after a chmod by hand. postinst sets 0600 on every configure, which corrects
    an existing stage on upgrade. A write as root (an operator running phis) gives the file the owner
    and group of the file it replaces, or of config/, so the stage account can still read it.
  * Packaging: an upgrade restarts every running phis@<stage> instance once the new release is in
    place; remove stops them; purge drops their wants links and leaves the phis account and /srv/phis,
    the stages' data. The installation guide and the CLI reference ship under /usr/share/doc/phis.
  * Packaging: a stop is no failure; the unit takes the server's exit status 143 on SIGTERM as success.
    Purge removes the proxy templates postinst copied, unless changed or enabled.
  * INSTALL: without NodeSource, apt install stops on the unmet nodejs dependency (noble carries 18).

 -- Phisys Ltd. <debian@phisys.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:43:25 +0000

